{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0<y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-105176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-105176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-105176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-105176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2<x<0"] ["math" "-2<x<2"] ["math" "-2\\le x<0"] ["math" "0<x<2"] ["math" "0<x\\le 2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-105176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2<x<0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/cdca164d343d8bff4c78a1e366e52c588ca6c54dfdea61acea1900bcbdc79f31.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and II are false. As we have seen, $A$ contains all its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161625" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -1+x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/3e7d8c11ac4b3de8473741a362ad2b78555c764da2d61f955435e8d59771cf46.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. As we've seen, $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∂A$\n- $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/4540e03fc5404474a0cd900c89004e6a5cfe7ac2d4702348e9d0395fc1c914e9.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/2a93b912f0d7b3a84bf0ec9c3b3596d080a9e71a345ff436e2f591edf042d9db.png)\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $A=\\text{int}\\,A$ or, equivalently,  $A-\\text{int}\\,A=∅.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂{R}^{2}-A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and  III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4y>{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- $∂A⊂A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/a380742f47d97062d56b482592cd2d2961dcc40262131a99886b815c507ab6e3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/26d264d702368ed6fe05577d7c34630bd16b41bdba8d206dd4db39763db02938.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊈A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and  II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- $∂A⊂A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/62c410c21e79e1bc688c1ff1a3440a207c62bcad42525bdc93fa2770b76d48bd.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/assets/33a4738b642443c2535d347aa53ee2b7b80c800142c4844d94578769118ebfbc.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅,$ where $∅$ denotes the empty set.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{int}\\,A$ contains all points in $A$ except the boundary points, we must have $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points, so we must have $∂A⊂A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb36c5b3c2f178f2e0b801"} {"question" "q-161444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e9e0af57d11aa61b8e1486c4935f1be8908aaf5f8d0cdd39c79afc9a8917909"} {"question" "q-161444" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041552/state.json" "file_sha256" "5579d886d8cbf4dc8afab9f4e3d2db81c23d80d306fb